      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Introduction\n\nSome texts in History Tracers end with an exercise. It is a short activity that helps you check whether you understood the main ideas. This guide explains how to answer an exercise and also shows where to find the games of the project.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_how",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### How the exercise works\n\nAn exercise is made of questions with the options **Yes** and **No**. Choose the option you think is correct and click the **Check** button to see the result. History Tracers then marks whether your answer is right and explains the correct one. To clear your answers and try again, click the **New** button. The exercise at the end of this page is an example: answer it and click **Check** to see the result.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_games",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Games\n\nHistory Tracers also offers games. Each one has its own rules, explained on the game's page, and you can reach them through the **Games** menu on the sidebar. The games are a way to learn by practising.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_conclusion",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Conclusion\n\nExercises and games invite you to learn by doing. Answer the exercise below and explore the **Games** menu to discover the activities of the project.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      }
   ],
